```javascript
module.exports.EventEmitter = class EventEmitter {
  constructor() {
    this.events = {};
  }

  on(event, handler) {
    if (!this.events[event]) {
      this.events[event] = [];
    }
    this.events[event].push({ handler, once: false });
    return this;
  }

  off(event, handler) {
    if (!this.events[event]) return this;
    this.events[event] = this.events[event].filter(
      listener => listener.handler !== handler
    );
    return this;
  }

  once(event, handler) {
    if (!this.events[event]) {
      this.events[event] = [];
    }
    this.events[event].push({ handler, once: true });
    return this;
  }

  emit(event, ...args) {
    if (!this.events[event]) return this;
    this.events[event] = this.events[event].filter(listener => {
      listener.handler(...args);
      return !listener.once;
    });
    return this;
  }
};
```

**Key features:**
- `on()` and `once()` register listeners; `off()` removes by handler reference
- `emit()` calls all listeners with provided args, automatically removing one-time listeners after execution
- All methods return `this` for optional chaining
- Stores listeners with metadata to track which are one-time

